<title>USA: U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS -- Issues to watch.</title>
<headline>U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS -- Issues to watch.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>* Healthsouth Corp and Horizon/CMS Healthcare Corp said Tuesday they had agreed to merge in a stock swap valued at about $1.6 billion. Healthsouth closed at 43-1/8 Friday while Horizon closed at 14-1/4.</p>
<p>* H.F. Ahmanson and Co said it had made an unsolicited bid for Great Western Financial Corp valued at nearly $6 billion, or about $42.53 a share. Ahmanson closed at 40-1/2. Great Western finished at 34-1/4.  </p>
<p>* Marriott International Inc said it would acquire Renaissance Hotel Group N.V. for $30 a share. Marriott said the deal was valued at about $1 billion, including debt assumption. Marriott closed at 55-1/4 while Renaissance finished at 25-1/8.</p>
<p>* Apple Computer Inc Chairman Gilbert Amelio said restructuring measures to be announced next month would cut costs by $400 million a year. The stock closed at 16-5/16.</p>
